## Luminescent multifunctional lanthanides-based metal–organic frameworks†
## 1. Introduction
Luminescent materials, or phosphors, find applications in cathode ray tubes, projection televisions, fluorescent
tubes and X-ray detectors. Lanthanide \((\mathrm{Ln}^{3+})\) -doped materials are of great interest for a wide range of other photonic applications, such as tunable lasers, light-emitting diodes, low-energy scintillators, amplifiers for optical communications and optical storage. Moreover, \(\mathrm{Ln}^{3+}\) -based complexes are very promising for efficient light conversion molecular devices, on account of their potential applications such as luminescent labels for fluoro-immunoassays, light concentrators for photovoltaic devices, antennae in
